# Frontend Theme

For work under `apps/web`, read `docs/frontend-implementation.md`, `docs/frontend-theme.md`, and root `AGENTS.md` before changing UI.

Rules:

- Nuxt 4 + Vue 3 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS is the frontend stack; Nuxt UI v4 is the required component foundation.
- Before creating a generic primitive, inspect existing shared components and the current official Nuxt UI catalog.
- Use `https://nuxt.com/llms.txt` for unfamiliar Nuxt APIs/best practices.
- Use the configured Nuxt UI MCP server for unfamiliar component props, slots, events, examples and metadata.
- Do not hand-roll a generic primitive when Nuxt UI provides the component or a documented composition.
- A custom primitive requires explicit justification identifying the Nuxt UI options checked, why they are insufficient, and the accessibility/interaction behavior provided.
- Product components compose Nuxt UI; do not put Agent Board backend/domain ownership into generic presentation components.
- The visual language is dense and technical: neutral graphite surfaces, sparse muted steel-blue emphasis, thin borders and restrained/no shadows.
- Cards and large panels are square by default (`0px` radius). Inputs, buttons, menus, overlays and similar controls use at most `0-2px` radius unless interaction semantics justify otherwise.
- Do not introduce generic `rounded-lg`/`rounded-xl`, soft floating cards, or pill-shaped controls as a default design treatment.
- Pill shapes are reserved for cases where the shape conveys useful semantics such as tags/chips/statuses.
- Prefer tonal surface hierarchy and borders over shadows for depth.
- Use shared Nuxt UI theme/component defaults and semantic colors rather than scattered raw palette values.
- Primary/accent color is a restrained steel blue and should be used sparingly for active navigation, links, primary actions, selection and focus.
- Dark mode is default; light mode remains fully supported and retains the same square technical visual language.
- Preserve semantic HTML and readable hierarchy for headings, body text, status/meta text, logs and code.
- Preserve accessibility, keyboard/focus behavior and responsive behavior provided by Nuxt UI/Reka UI.
- Muted text/borders still need sufficient readability and contrast; status never relies on color alone.
- Nuxt/Nitro server facilities do not own Agent Board domain state. Durable product state, scheduling, execution and authorization remain Go-owned.
- Live Run/Issue UI reconciles against persisted API/SSE state.
- Theme changes use TDD according to `docs/testing.md`.
